{"seq":32,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w25216"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish-mge card ppm-109, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Physiology and Anatomy] What are the gaps between nerve cells called?\nA. Axons B. Dendrites C. Synapses\nAnswer: C. Synapses are the small gaps between nerve cells (neurons). They play a crucial role in transmitting signals from one neuron to another, facilitating neural communication throughout the nervous system.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/mythology, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, earth-space/a","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish-mge/ppm-109.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"What are the junctions between nerve cells, where signals pass from one neuron to the next, called?"},{"field":"de","new":"Wie heißen die Verbindungsstellen zwischen Nervenzellen, an denen Signale von einem Neuron zum nächsten übertragen werden?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish-mge","card":"ppm-109","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Physiology and Anatomy] What are the gaps between nerve cells called?\nA. Axons B. Dendrites C. Synapses\nAnswer: C. Synapses are the small gaps between nerve cells (neurons). They play a crucial role in transmitting signals from one neuron to another, facilitating neural communication throughout the nervous system."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f01122"}],"hash":"ffdb389da302"},
